WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.428
Fictional Meridian teaching case No course example grants workplace

00:00:05.468 --> 00:00:11.389
authority Requests and unverified claims are not approvals Which

00:00:11.442 --> 00:00:15.363
option would you recommend to Lindiwe Explain what it

00:00:15.428 --> 00:00:18.849
preserves what it may change and which confirmations are

00:00:18.928 --> 00:00:19.613
still needed

00:00:19.773 --> 00:00:24.300
An operations-led discussion may preserve the morning plan Daniel

00:00:24.379 --> 00:00:27.392
could recommend that the appointed operations owner handle the

00:00:27.432 --> 00:00:32.313
supplier discussion This would protect Lindiwe’s preparation and decision

00:00:32.313 --> 00:00:35.484
meeting but only if the discussion falls within that

00:00:35.563 --> 00:00:40.234
person’s delegation and the person accepts the assignment Lindiwe’s

00:00:40.274 --> 00:00:44.879
approval must also be obtained where required These conditions

00:00:44.932 --> 00:00:47.168
are not supplied as confirmed facts

00:00:47.695 --> 00:00:52.090
A later appointment may avoid the current conflict Daniel

00:00:52.156 --> 00:00:55.063
could investigate a later slot for Lindiwe and ask

00:00:55.129 --> 00:00:58.813
when the supplier actually needs the decision He must

00:00:58.853 --> 00:01:02.958
check availability the supplier’s acceptance and the latest useful

00:01:03.011 --> 00:01:07.827
decision time before recommending a particular arrangement A possible

00:01:07.932 --> 00:01:10.156
slot is not a confirmed appointment

00:01:10.689 --> 00:01:14.386
A change to the protected commitments needs Lindiwe’s decision

00:01:15.268 --> 00:01:19.373
If Lindiwe considers changing the morning plan Daniel explains

00:01:19.413 --> 00:01:21.623
the preparation time that would be lost and the

00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:25.728
effects on other participants and papers He asks for

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:28.755
the authorised decision rather than treating the change as

00:01:28.847 --> 00:01:30.728
routine diary administration

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:35.321
The supplier’s claim does not confirm the appointment The

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:38.913
supplier says that 09:45 has been approved but the

00:01:38.953 --> 00:01:41.887
approval has not been verified and the slot conflicts

00:01:41.926 --> 00:01:46.176
with two commitments Daniel must keep the appointment pending

00:01:46.518 --> 00:01:49.558
check the claim with the appointed decision-maker and explain

00:01:49.624 --> 00:01:50.426
the conflict

00:01:50.947 --> 00:01:54.789
An incorrect impression of confirmation needs a visible correction

00:01:55.671 --> 00:01:58.644
If Daniel has already sent a message that implies

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.908
the slot is confirmed he explains the correction to

00:02:01.947 --> 00:02:05.881
the affected recipients the slot remains pending the claimed

00:02:05.908 --> 00:02:09.092
approval is being checked and the conflicts still need

00:02:09.092 --> 00:02:13.171
a decision He updates the current controlled record so

00:02:13.223 --> 00:02:16.250
that people do not act on the earlier misunderstanding

00:02:17.144 --> 00:02:20.631
Quietly replacing an attachment would not reliably correct what

00:02:20.697 --> 00:02:21.829
recipients believe
